=== USER (turn 2) ===
Good questions — let me answer all of them so you can just build.

1. **Severity coverage** — yes, there is a Sev2. If production is down or degraded *but a viable workaround exists*, that's Sev2. Engineering is needed for Sev2 as well, same as Sev1. Anything that doesn't hit Sev1 or Sev2 conditions falls to Sev3. So: no workaround → Sev1 (if Enterprise + prod down) or escalate accordingly; workaround available → Sev2; no production impact at all → Sev3.

2. **`businessImpact`** — treat it as a pass-through. It gets recorded on the case (carried through for context) but the severity decision is driven entirely by the structured fields. No AI interpretation node needed.

3. **`customerTier` values** — the valid tiers are **Enterprise**, **Business**, and **Standard**. Enterprise is the only tier that can trigger Sev1 under our policy; the others follow the same Sev2/Sev3 logic based on production status and workaround availability.

4. **Trigger** — treat it as a standalone entry point invoked externally (API call or direct invocation). The grader will run it directly with seeded inputs, so just make sure the entry point accepts the declared inputs cleanly.

5. **Downstream of "Draft"** — `responseMode = "Draft"` is purely an output flag for the downstream system to act on. No Action Center step or human approval task inside this flow itself.

That should cover everything — go ahead and build it.

